  "$comment": "The pre-cleared name parts (docs/ai-layer.md, ad-inventory and 3.2). Every startup and player name is a head and a tail, or an adjective and a noun, composed by src/content/composer.ts; no free-form name exists. Each part passed the brand and people blocklist, the offensive-word filter and the content lint alone; words that are the name of a tech, robotics, transport or fintech company the authoring agent knew of were left out by hand (animals stay in the player pools only, because '<animal> AI' is the commonest real startup pattern). On 2026-10-20 the AI-jargon heads (Token, Prompt, Cache, Shard, Vibe, Waitlist, Standup, Roadmap, Seedling) were dropped and seventeen heads the agent suspected were searched and dropped as conflicts (see 'removed'); the remaining parts were not web-searched one by one; the composed pairs that fail the lint are in banned-pairs.json. The kits that used a removed head got new pairs; six of those names were spot-searched on 2026-10-20 (\"Kiosk Metrics\": only a dashboard feature of a venue-mapping product, no company; \"Spool Works\", \"Turnip Systems\", \"Teaspoon Systems\", \"Gondola Drones\", \"Lanyard Logic\": nothing found).",
